decisions.description:
THREE searches have now been run and all fourteen are recorded in the tracker with their method and result (see the recovery record on the Rules page). The third read the authoritative business scope document, EJE_Master_Scope_and_Audit_Baseline_v2.docx, which docs/SCOPE.md names as the scope of record and which had never been opened: its items 11-24 are topic headings (Checklists, Parts Delivery Note, Media and Technical Library, ...), not rules, and it contains no rule register at all.

NO WORDING NUMBERED 11-24 EXISTS IN ANY ACCESSIBLE SOURCE.

THIRTY-TWO standing rules have been recovered verbatim and are in force, none of them numbered:
  - SCOPE-P01…SCOPE-P09 - the scope document's §2 product objective and principles;
  - SCOPE-D01…SCOPE-D08 - its §28 development control rules;
  - PRIN-01…PRIN-14 - the founding instruction's ARCHITECTURAL PRINCIPLES;
  - STAND-01 - the owner's MOST IMPORTANT RULE.

Any of these could be what rules 11-24 refer to, and the tracker will not choose: assigning a number to a rule on a resemblance is the fabrication the rules forbid. The numbers stay SOURCE_MISSING, with the search recorded, until the owner resolves it.

DECIDED 26 September 2026 by the project owner: the wording is unrecoverable, the numbers stay SOURCE_MISSING, the recovered principles are NOT to be renumbered into them, and the gap is not to be closed silently. The question and all four options above are kept exactly as they were asked.
